  "id": "Compound::DB00247 - Gene::3351",
  "verbalization": "Methysergide, a serotoninergic agent, is shown to interact with Htr1e and Htr6, both of which participate in serotonin receptor signaling. This suggests that Methysergide may influence serotonin receptor activity through these intermediaries. Htr1b, a receptor that participates in serotonin receptor signaling, is thus positioned as a downstream target of Methysergide through the shared pathway of serotonin receptor engagement. The evidence is consistent with Methysergide acting as a modulator of serotonin receptor function, potentially through Htr1e or Htr6, which in turn interact with Htr1b. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where Methysergide may exert its effects by modulating serotonin receptor activity, with Htr1b being a key downstream effector. The observed scores support a direct relationship, but the exact nature of the interaction remains inferred through the shared participation in receptor signaling.",
